# Line endings — LF everywhere, in the repo and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, tools running under WSL/Windows can rewrite a file to CRLF,
# which turns a one-line change into a whole-file diff. It happened twice in a
# single session: a one-line addition to chart-manager.js showed up as 174
# changed lines, and a one-line id fix in five algorithm JSONs as ~354 lines
# each. `text=auto` still lets Git detect binary content and leave it alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF regardless of detection — CRLF breaks the shebang.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never convert, never diff as text.
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.otf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.xlsx binary
